# Proof-run evidence is deliberately NOT committed.
#
# The screenshots and frame PNGs contain Google Maps Content. Google Maps
# Platform ToS §3.2.3(a)/(b) prohibit storing, re-hosting or re-sharing that
# Content, and the Map Tiles API policies prohibit "Offline uses". Keeping the
# evidence on the machine that produced it — and citing it by path in
# docs/repair/product-proof-sprint/27b/REPORT.md — is the conservative reading.
#
# Everything that is safe to keep (camera parameters, request counts, timings,
# attribution strings) lives in summary.json, which IS committed.
#
# Both directories below are created on demand by their harness
# (run-proof.mjs writes proof/evidence/, bakeoff/run.mjs creates
# bakeoff/results/frames/ at startup), so neither exists in a clean checkout.
# That is not a stale rule: the ignore has to be in place BEFORE the run that
# produces the files, or the first run commits Google Maps Content.
evidence/*.png
bakeoff/results/frames/
# Blinded comparison sets are resampled crops OF those frames, so they are the
# same Content by another name. The scoring artefacts beside them (VERDICT.md,
# KEY.json, GROUPS.json) are text and ARE committed — the verdict is the
# evidence, the pixels were only how it was reached.
bakeoff/results/blind-*/*.png
# Same rule for the evaluation matrix and the starved-session check: the frame
# PNGs are provider imagery, the report.json beside them is camera parameters,
# timings, request counts and pixel statistics, and only the latter is safe to
# commit.
eval-matrix/**/*.png
empty-frame-guard/*.png
